{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966790,"nonce":"z+vwLuejmurMNGpDOe2JSNMRF50=","title":"fast-path region re-walk drew motion regions at DPI² — oversized slider/switch ghost near","message":"Symptom: hovering a radio made sliders and the switch lose their fill\nand thumb while one oversized (2×) copy drew at doubled coordinates\nnear the pointer. Looked like a \"ghost\", was actually **relocation**:\nthe compositor fast path re-emits every `MotionSubtree` region via\n`collect_dynamic_region_primitives`, and that re-walk pushed the DPI\nscale around an ambient affine that already contains DPI (measured:\nevery region's ambient reads `sx = scale_factor`). 2×2 = 4× physical\n= 2× logical, positions doubled with it.\n\nA second, compounding variant in the same path: the re-walk also\n**re-recorded** regions, so ambient went 2→4→8 across frames (probe:\n`SCALED-REGION`). Fixed with `set_region_capture_suppressed` — the\nwalker emits without recording during a re-walk; the main walk's\nregions are the only correct ones. The `CssAnimated`/`Canvas`\nexclusions in that collect were earlier point-fixes for the same\ndisease.\n\nWhy it looked hover/transform/disabled-dependent (five wrong theories):\nthe fast path only runs for **pure visual updates with no rebuild**.\nRadios with a hover FSM rebuilt on hover → slow path → correct.\nThe disabled radio (no FSM transition consumed) and later all radios\n(after `NoState`) repainted via state styles alone → fast path →\nartifact. The CSS `:hover` transform was a bystander throughout; it is\nback in and fine.\n\nRules learned, cheaply next time:\n- If content is *missing from its true position* while a wrong-scale\n  copy appears, think \"one draw at the wrong transform\", not \"cache\n  ghost\".\n- 2× on a 2× DPI screen is DPI applied twice. Grep the path between\n  ambient capture and re-emission for a second `scale_factor` push.\n- Probe before naming a cause. Frames (`ffmpeg fps=6` + tile) and an\n  affine probe on `dynamic_regions` found this; five code-shape\n  theories in a row did not.\n\nRelated: [[gotcha-canvas-fast-path-freeze]],\n[[gotcha-composite-scratch-hash-layer-commands]].","files":null}]}